I get really nervous and I can hardly speak.

25
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:26,600
Well, I must confess that I am a bit claustrophobic.

26
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,060
I hate being in an elevator for more than five seconds.

27
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,680
We are such weirdos, right?

28
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:43,520
All right, we're back, so let's take a look at those phobias on Language Takeaway.

29
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,400
Language Takeaway.

30
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:49,500
The first phobia that we have is called aerophobia.

31
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,280
That's right, aerophobia.

32
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:54,020
That means that you are scared of flying.

33
00:01:55,120 --> 00:02:00,180
We can tell because phobia means fear of something, but it's not just a fear.

34
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:04,920
It means that if you go on an airplane, you get very, very upset.

35
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:07,800
You think that you're going to die.

36
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:12,850
Phobia is a very serious fear, but aero, like aeroplane, is the prefix.

37
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:16,360
Phobia is a fear of going on airplanes.

38
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:16,590
That's right.

39
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,170
Another phobia that we have is arachnophobia.

40
00:02:20,830 --> 00:02:25,350
Again, as you see in the prefix, arachno is related to a spider.

41
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:26,230
That's right.

42
00:02:26,510 --> 00:02:28,870
This comes from the origins of English.

43
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:35,590
I'm not sure if it's Greek or Latin, but arachnophobia, like arachnid, has to do with spiders.

44
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:40,400
I'm afraid of spiders if I have arachnophobia.

45
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:43,160
That is right.

46
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:48,780
Now taking a look at two more types of phobias here, we have acrophobia and glossophobia.

47
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:51,220
Let's take a look at the first one, acrophobia.

48
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,450
Acrophobia has to do with heights.

49
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,950
I don't like to be on tall buildings.

50
00:02:57,120 --> 00:03:00,010
I don't like to maybe look down from heights.

51
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,230
That means I'm afraid of heights.

52
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:01,870
That's right.

53
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:05,710
You're afraid of being at a very high altitude, acrophobia.

54
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:14,810
Now glossophobia is an interesting one because this one, you are scared of public speaking or you get very nervous when you're in front of a group of people.

55
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:15,330
Right.

56
00:03:15,490 --> 00:03:21,790
So this is actually a very, very common fear, but if it's a serious fear, it's a phobia.

57
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:31,120
So glossophobia means that when you go in front of people, you get very, very anxious, upset, your stomach hurts, you have wet hands.

58
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,880
So that's a very serious fear.

59
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:33,170
That's right.

60
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:37,370
And for our last phobia, we have claustrophobia.

61
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:39,440
I think it's one of the most common ones.

62
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:44,200
If you have claustrophobia, you're afraid of smaller tight spaces.

63
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:44,330
That's right.

64
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:56,520
So people who, so you heard the word claustrophobic, people who are claustrophobic or people who suffer from claustrophobia don't like to be in small tight places like elevators, for example, tunnels.

65
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:00,360
So now you brought up an interesting point.

66
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:10,800
Our last phobia, we said claustrophobic and now we must make the difference between, for example, claustrophobia and being claustrophobic.

67
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:19,160
So a phobia, you hear the word, you hear the ending IA, phobia, claustrophobia is a noun.

68
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:23,280
That means I can talk about, I have it, I have this fear.

69
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:28,910
But when you're talking about the adjective, something that describes you, you would have to use the ic ending.

70
00:04:29,290 --> 00:04:30,450
I'm claustrophobic.

71
00:04:31,030 --> 00:04:32,310
He is acrophobic.

72
00:04:32,810 --> 00:04:34,250
They are aerophobic.

73
00:04:34,850 --> 00:04:37,410
Okay, so that is the adjective form.

74
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:44,200
So if I say I have arachnophobia, it means I have this fear or I can say I am arachnophobic.

75
00:04:44,950 --> 00:04:45,200
Great.

76
00:04:45,450 --> 00:04:47,730
So this can be used for all other kinds of phobias.

77
00:04:48,030 --> 00:04:50,430
So when you learn those words, remember that there's two different kinds.

78
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:56,030
There's the IA, there's the IA, a phobia, which is the noun and ic, which is the adjective.

79
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,240
All right.

